  "hints": [
    "A hash map finds an entry in O(1) but forgets the order of use. A list remembers the order but needs O(n) to find an entry. You need both.",
    "Keep the entries in a doubly linked list, most recently used at one end, and a map from key to list node. A hit unlinks the node and relinks it at the front; an eviction drops the node at the other end.",
    "In JavaScript a Map iterates in insertion order. Deleting a key and setting it again moves it to the end, so map.keys().next().value is always the least recently used key."
  ],
  "complexity": {"time":"O(1) for get and put","space":"O(capacity)"}
